# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_symbol_use_recall.py" "SYMBOL-USE RECALL GATE: PASS" "symbol-use recall (base-type + constructor uses captured as calls-class edges)" "symbol-use recall: a file that EXTENDS/IMPLEMENTS a base type or CONSTRUCTS a type (new Foo() / Go composite literal / Rust struct expr) DEPENDS on the defining file with NO plain calls edge -- the call graph missed it (measured: +13.9 pts co-change recall on a real C# repo, 1752 newly-CORROBORATED namespace edges on jellyfin, exactly PR #253's finding that C#/Go wire via constructor/inheritance not calls). Captured as calls-CLASS edges (dst = the USED TYPE NAME, content-free) so they resolve to the defining file through the SAME _claim_adjacency precision machinery every call edge already passes: defs_ok<=3 fan-out cap, import-confirmation, single-definer, hub dampening, prod->test guard -- that existing guard set is what bounds precision (a ubiquitous type defined in >3 files cannot fan out a decoy). PRECISION-SCOPED to base + constructor ONLY (NOT broad param/field type annotations, measured catastrophically noisy for ~zero recall). Proven across 8 languages on KNOWN-TRUTH fixtures: RECALL (a cross-file base/ctor use produces a resolvable calls-class edge + lands the user in the type-definer's blast radius) AND PRECISION (a >3-definer ubiquitous type is emitted honestly but the engine's defs_ok cap stops it fanning out; a constructor ARGUMENT is never a type use)" "symbol-use recall: base-type + constructor uses become calls-class edges to the defining file (recall the call graph missed -- C#/Go #253 case), bounded by the engine's existing defs_ok/import-confirmation guards (precision); 8 languages, content-free" 20
